ref 17592186045417] [17592186420014 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420014 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420014 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cf591f90-dd66-50c4-8cda-a517404994ce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420015 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420015 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420015 #edb/ref 1077 "field-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420015 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420015 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d666e47f-869a-5aac-9dd7-a42fc1d1dec8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420016 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420016 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420016 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420016 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420016 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420016 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e14fbafa-f0bc-5fe2-bb94-563a8f48a64a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420017 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420017 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420017 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420017 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420017 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420017 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e6148daf-4057-5d9a-8a64-641f2d763dc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420018 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420018 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420018 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420018 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186419988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420018 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420018 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420018 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420018 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186419983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420018 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ecccfb9f-b179-57da-b516-7c00246e405b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420008 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420019 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420019 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420019 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420019 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-axis is a {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-axis is a {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420019 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2b822a97-2fd4-5c06-914f-271b7726501f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420019 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nRecall that a homogeneous system of linear differential equations has a single equilibrium (fixed point) at the origin.\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $x$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis and also approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $y$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a stable node (sink)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/1c/1c4133695eeb868f563f80021755fea75bef622e1ad46cbbf6daff1c953cb075.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420020 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420020 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332594" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420020 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420020 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=3x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=7y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420020 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d431d34-43bf-517f-a3a4-67b126780182" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420020 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=7$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{7t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{7t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/e9/e9fa4226361b8c0abe6c5b02374967b025aa8870757150f86b15434841825e2d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420021 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420021 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420021 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420021 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333211" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420021 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420021 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below regarding the given decoupled system of linear differential equations.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $x$-axis is a {{field-1}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe $y$-axis is a {{field-2}} line.\n\n$\\,$\nThe equilibrium point (origin) is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420021 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "637ffaff-c65f-5c9b-99c9-53a0db0e19a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420021 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nRecall that a homogeneous system of linear differential equations has a single equilibrium (fixed point) at the origin.\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{5t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis and move away from the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $x$-axis is the $\\text{unstable}$ line.\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4$ with the eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ The corresponding straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, the $y$-axis is the $\\text{stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a saddle point}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/ae/ae1135571904a4bfb49eb79e187fa6d1754fc562fe66b604d33eb555418a1345.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420022 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420022 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420022 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420022 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-2x(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-6y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could represent the phase portrait of the decoupled system above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420022 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "677c9e5d-972e-57a9-95d7-9e9c75c0d58d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420022 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]x(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSince our system is decoupled, its eigenvectors are the following:\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2}=-6$ with the corresponding eigenvector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-6t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, notice that:\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x$-axis. Since ${e}^{-2t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\n- The straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-6t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $y$-axis. Since ${e}^{-6t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nAmong the given options, the only phase portrait satisfying these conditions is the following:\n\n![](images/b9/b99c7dc98a7a43dabb0fb7222fd6b4eeaaec727bc180953ee24769389667c501.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
